  m_Name: SeaScallop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HiddenHarbours.Fishing::HiddenHarbours.Fishing.FishEcologyDef
  Id: "ecology.sea_scallop"
  SpeciesId: "fish.sea_scallop"
  ScientificName: "Placopecten magellanicus"
  LifeStageAndScope: "Post-larval fishable coastal animals; typical reference habitat only. Adults unless the notes explicitly distinguish juveniles."
  TypicalMinDepthMetres: 15
  TypicalMaxDepthMetres: 110
  DepthEvidence: "Authored subtidal reference band for commercial beds on sand and gravel; both endpoints are provisional authoring values."
  Layer: 3
  Habitats: 10
  PreferredVegetation: 0
  VegetationEvidence: "The cited profile does not establish a species-wide eelgrass or kelp preference; zero means no preference inferred, not avoidance."
  Grouping: 2
  DayHabit: 5
  TideHabit: 1
  HabitEvidence: "A subtidal filter feeder that is never bared by the tide, so no tide gate is inferred; no daylight presence gate is inferred."
  BiologyNotes: "Adults lie in dense beds on sand and gravel and can swim short distances by clapping their valves, so they are a loose benthic aggregation, not a cemented bed. Larval dispersal is outside its scope."
